commit 9615349df7e767bb76d48d1b2aee0087f9307e5f

C03: playing a video or a song on YouTube runs the local player and the reply names the observed title (MUSIC1553)

MUSIC1078 left the YouTube literals without an individual link: media.play.youtube existed (yt-dlp resolves the first result, mpv plays it; both installed on this PC) but the receipt carried the query as the title, the reviewed conductor never proposed the playback and the mind bound no query. YouTubeMpvAdapter now prints the resolved video's title before the stream URL and carries it in the receipt (titleObserved); ProductConductorHost proposes media.play.youtube to the root reviewer like the captures and the page read; the mind binds the query with the person's own words minus a leading article (youtube_play_query: «video de lofi», «cancion de michael jackson»; the reader also admits «reproducí»/«poné»), the composer projects query/title/state, instructs the report to say it is playing and quote the observed title verbatim, vetoes any unobserved title or a question (youtube_unobserved_title, youtube_question) and accepts «se reproduce» as the playing state. The constraint acknowledgement prompt excludes a trailing question. Registry-wide recogniser diff with the real Start catalog: no literal changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


